---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeExample from "../../components/CodeExample.astro";
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";

const stringExample = `webata { nwereEriri, maliteNa, kwụsịNa, ogologoEriri, jikọọEriri, wepuOghere, okwuNta, okwuNnukwu, dochieEriri } site na "kwechiri:eriri"

bipụta(nwereEriri("Kwechiri", "chiri"))
bipụta(maliteNa("Kwechiri", "Kwe"))
bipụta(kwụsịNa("Kwechiri", "chiri"))
bipụta(ogologoEriri("Ụbọchị"))
bipụta(jikọọEriri("Kwe", "chiri"))
bipụta(wepuOghere("  Kwechiri  "))
bipụta(okwuNta("ỤBỌCHỊ"))
bipụta(okwuNnukwu("ọma"))
bipụta(dochieEriri("Kwechiri", "chiri", "Kwe"))`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Standard Library"
  description="The official Kwechiri string module and its nine functions."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Documentation"
    title="Explicit imports, specified behavior."
    lead="Batch 11A introduced the reserved kwechiri: namespace. Batches 11B and 11C extend its pure string module with inspection, measurement, and transformation."
  />

  <div class="shell content-layout">
    <DocsNav />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2><code>kwechiri:eriri</code></h2>
      <p>
        The module exports nine functions. All are pure,
        non-mutating, case-sensitive, and free of implicit coercion or
        normalization.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Function</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>nwereEriri</code></td><td><code>(string, string) -&gt; boolean</code></td><td>Contains</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>maliteNa</code></td><td><code>(string, string) -&gt; boolean</code></td><td>Starts with</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>kwụsịNa</code></td><td><code>(string, string) -&gt; boolean</code></td><td>Ends with</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ogologoEriri</code></td><td><code>(string) -&gt; number</code></td><td>Grapheme-cluster length</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>jikọọEriri</code></td><td><code>(string, string) -&gt; string</code></td><td>Exact concatenation</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>wepuOghere</code></td><td><code>(string) -&gt; string</code></td><td>Trim surrounding whitespace</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>okwuNta</code></td><td><code>(string) -&gt; string</code></td><td>Unicode lowercase</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>okwuNnukwu</code></td><td><code>(string) -&gt; string</code></td><td>Unicode uppercase</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>dochieEriri</code></td><td><code>(string, string, string) -&gt; string</code></td><td>Literal replace all</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <CodeExample
        label="Standard Library"
        code={stringExample}
        output={"eziokwu\neziokwu\neziokwu\n6\nKwechiri\nKwechiri\nụbọchị\nỌMA\nKweKwe"}
      />

      <h2>Exact string behavior</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Matching is case-sensitive and exact.</li>
        <li>String contents are not normalized.</li>
        <li>The empty string is contained in every string and is a prefix and suffix of every string.</li>
        <li><code>ogologoEriri</code> counts user-perceived characters; an Igbo letter with combining marks counts once.</li>
        <li><code>jikọọEriri</code> joins exact raw sequences without inserting separators.</li>
        <li><code>wepuOghere</code> removes only surrounding Unicode whitespace.</li>
        <li>Case conversion uses locale-independent Unicode mapping without normalization.</li>
        <li><code>dochieEriri</code> replaces every exact non-overlapping occurrence literally.</li>
        <li>Wrong arity and statically known wrong argument types are located semantic errors.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout callout--gold">
        <strong>The original five names are frozen for 1.0.</strong>
        Batch 11C adds four approved transformation functions.
      </div>

      <p>
        Read the
        <a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/standard-library/README.md`}>Standard Library documentation</a>
        and
        <a href={`${SITE.github}/tree/main/docs/design-decisions`}>ADR-020 through ADR-023</a>
        for the full contract.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
